-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Gauntlet
  Publisher   U.S. Gold, 1986
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (all of these files together):

  File        Gauntlet (1986)(US Gold)(Side A).tzx
  MD5         51cc150a2cf4db091f61764d1156110e
  File        Gauntlet (1986)(US Gold)(Side B).tzx
  MD5         2c64dd178f2dab735f002f066cdba2ca

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.1: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing
              1.3: eight cheats from the archive's POKEs, off by default; the
              heroes' and the monsters' shots are Next sprites in their
              shooter's colour (Thor red-orange, Thyra ice blue, Merlin gold,
              Questor leaf green, demons' fireballs amber, lobbers' rocks
              sandstone), so they no longer show the scenery's colours or a
              block of wall colour when they cross a wall

  Note        The whole game from both tape sides with no loading: the main
              game and all 31 level blocks come from memory. The play window
              is painted tiles on the tile layer and the panel is painted on
              Layer 2; the game underneath is unchanged. All four heroes are
              painted, and the heroes' and monsters' shots are sprites in
              their shooter's colour. Steady speed (off by default): 28 MHz
              with an update every 3 frames. Keys: Space through the title,
              credits and instructions; then the cursor keys move the pointer
              and Space picks players, hero and controls (Sinclair, Kempston,
              Protek or keyboard). Keyboard: player 1 up 1, down Q, left S,
              right D, fire Z, magic Caps Shift; player 2 up 8, down I, left
              K, right L, fire M, magic Space; P pauses. Known issues: a few
              cells where things overlap, and the high score and name entry
              text, keep their Spectrum colours.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite health
   2  Infinite keys
   3  Infinite magic bottles
   4  Infinite treasure time
   5  Shoot through walls
   6  Infinite amulet's effect
   7  No enemy generation
   8  No non-generated enemies

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

