-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification of the main game's hooks on
              three recordings, and of the shots on two; the hand-over from
              the front end and the level blocks from memory by unit cases and
              a recording's real tape load; simulated boot of both builds; run
              in OverSpec from the title into level 1, one and two players.
              Played by the owner on a ZX Spectrum Next (KS3), 2026-11-27: 1.1
              good. 1.3 (shots as sprites, the cheats, Steady speed) played by
              the owner in OverSpec, 2026-11-28: good.

  Replay      NexClash differential verification of the main game's hooks on
              the rzxarchive's recordings of level blocks 1, 2 and 10 (61,548
              frames, 11,502 updates): every register and all game memory
              after each hook, the tile layer against the painted map after
              every update -> IDENTICAL. Level block 1 from memory equal to a
              recording's real tape load. The hand-over from the front end to
              the main game: unit case, and one broken build detected. 1.3
              shots: the main recording's 837 shots and 222 erased slots,
              3,202 updates over 15,698 frames identical; a block 2 run, 94
              shots in 1,900 frames, identical; every cheat subset at both
              speeds rebuilds byte for byte (512 builds).

  Emulator    OverSpec: from the title through the heroes' and controls
              screens into level 1, one and two players; blocks 2 and 10 with
              three and four shots on screen (349 shot pixels and 718 painted
              pixels around them matched); two players' shots through a
              painted wall with Shoot through walls; a tape playthrough to
              level 1 with Steady speed and two cheats; the owner played 1.3
              from the menu, 2026-11-28: good.

  Hardware    ZX Spectrum Next (Kickstarter 3), System/Next 26.11a: 1.1 played
              by the owner, good; 1.3 not yet run on hardware

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
